      "resolution_note": "LVMPD (ORI NV0020100) is a consolidated agency whose principal_jurisdiction_id in configs/consolidated_agency_footprints.csv is 32:municipal:place:3240000 (Las Vegas city), with geometry_source_type 'canonical_principal_place_plus_county_remainder' covering Las Vegas city plus unincorporated Clark County state-remainder BG shares, EXCLUDING excluded_place_geoids 3206500|3231900|3246000|3251800 (Boulder City, Henderson, Mesquite, North Las Vegas). HOWEVER: this pre-registration uses eb_jurisdiction_id, produced by src/crimerisk/allocation.py::_dominant_bg_jurisdiction operating directly on the raw geometric block_group_to_jurisdiction_crosswalk.parquet -- this function does NOT consume configs/consolidated_agency_footprints.csv at all (that file is only read inside _build_jurisdiction_component_allocations, several steps downstream, to retarget county-remainder allocation totals -- it never rewrites the BG-level jurisdiction tag). Verified: eb_jurisdiction_id == 32:municipal:place:3240000 selects 449 block groups, consistent with Las Vegas city's geometric place boundary alone (Henderson's 184 BGs at ~325k population is the nearest scale comparison; a full LVMPD consolidated Clark County footprint at ~2.3M population would imply roughly 1,150-1,300 BGs at the same density, an order of magnitude more than 449). CONCLUSION: the dominant eb_jurisdiction assignment does NOT reflect the LVMPD consolidated footprint -- it is the plain Las Vegas CITY place polygon only. This Batch C prediction therefore covers Las Vegas city proper (449 BGs), NOT the broader unincorporated-Clark-County area LVMPD actually polices. This is a narrower footprint than LVMPD's real service area and should be treated as a scope caveat when scoring against truth incident data, which may be reported at the LVMPD-consolidated-agency scale.",
