  "bg_jurisdiction_assignment_method": "Dominant BG assignment: eb_jurisdiction_id / eb_jurisdiction_type columns already present on the promoted block-group parquet, produced by src/crimerisk/allocation.py::_dominant_bg_jurisdiction (highest allocation_share per BG from state/geometry/block_group_to_jurisdiction_crosswalk.parquet). This is the same dominant-jurisdiction assignment the allocator uses elsewhere in the pipeline (e.g. for the EB jurisdiction prior). For each city, predicted_share is expected_count_<offense> for every BG with eb_jurisdiction_id == the city's jurisdiction_id, normalized to sum to 1 within that BG set. Cross-checked against the raw crosswalk allocation_share for exclusivity (see sanity_checks). NOTE (Las Vegas only): this method is purely geometric and does NOT incorporate configs/consolidated_agency_footprints.csv -- see the las_vegas_nv resolution_note for the full LVMPD footprint-scope caveat.",
